00:47:17.000 --> 00:48:09.000
that my mom gave me when I first moved out way back when and it's really stuck with me. Here's another fun tip. If you are buying new furniture, places like IKEA and some other big furniture stores, 90% of the time, someone is selling that exact thing that you want on Facebook marketplace. And maybe you'll have to pay to get it delivered, but that $50 extra that you're paying is saving you hundreds of dollars anyways. It's like 80 to 90% cheaper sometimes. I bought my desk this way. It was I think $170 brand new and I bought it for $25 in like off Facebook marketplace. IKEA also has a second hand section. You should go and look at that. There are so many good fines. I think you don't need to skimp. You don't need to not give yourself the things that you need

